  "summary_en": "This UK statutory instrument amends the Medical Devices Regulations 2002. It puts into effect EU Regulation 207/2012 on electronic instructions for use and EU Regulation 722/2012 on devices made with animal tissue. It updates the rules for CE marking, conformity assessment and notified bodies, and requires a review by 2019. It does not cover AI or robotics.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Makes the electronic-labelling requirements of Regulation (EU) 207/2012 enforceable in the UK",
   "Makes the animal-tissue device requirements of Regulation (EU) 722/2012 enforceable and removes duplicate UK rules",
   "Amends the CE marking and conformity assessment procedures for general and active implantable medical devices",
   "Updates EEA membership references and the mutual recognition agreements, including with Switzerland",
   "Requires the Secretary of State to review the regulations and publish a report by 31 December 2019"
  ],
